"groups":["b80496ad53a5642d","3ece676ec71590d3","71b2495735e2352d","83390b551c016789","2141b142249e70cc","ba29de40a22aea61","54249e0b3bc722b2"],"findings":"I read the change and did not run it, so every item below is **read**.\n\n1. **Pass `an` straight through instead of copying `timedOut` field by field** (`timeout-marker`: h2, h13, h14, h16, h17). Medium benefit, about 6 lines.\n   - `Analysis.timedOut` is copied into `AttentionView`, then into `CommitData.computed`, and re-listed by hand at each call site. `Analysis` already has `floor` and `derived`, so `attentionBlock(a.attention, an)` type-checks with no literal. That removes the h2 edit and makes `AttentionView` a `Pick<Analysis, 'floor'|'derived'|'timedOut'>`. The next field added to `Analysis` then needs no edits at the call sites.\n   - In `data.ts`, `computed: an ? { ...pick(an), below }` would do the same job.\n\n2. **Cut the extra `timedOutNote` export and string** (h21, h22). Small benefit, about 3 lines.\n   - `timedOutNote` is exported but used only inside `timedOutNotes`, so inline it or un-export it.\n   - `floorFrom` builds a different string for the same fact: `pattern: X (timed out: counted as matching)`. The test regexes already depend on both wordings.\n   - Use one phrase, `TIMED_OUT = 'timed out: counted as matching'`, across `show.ts`, `floorFrom` and the notes. Then the wording can't drift between surfaces.\n\n3. **Simplify the timed-out-first ordering in `floorFrom`** (h22). Small benefit, 2 lines.\n   - `[...top.filter(t), ...top.filter(!t)]` can be `top.sort((a, b) => +!!b.timedOut - +!!a.timedOut)`. `Array.prototype.sort` is stable, and `top` is already a fresh array from `filter`.\n\n4. **Replace the conditional spread when building a hit** (h20). Small benefit, 1 line.\n   - `...(timedOut ? { timedOut: true as const } : {})` can be `timedOut: timedOut || undefined`. `JSON.stringify` drops `undefined`, so `--json` output is unchanged. The `as const` cast goes away and the `timedOut?: true` type stays.\n\n5. **Fold the two git-failure helpers and the warning into one place** (`git-failure`: h5, h6). Small to medium benefit.\n   - `trustedRef` now needs `gitAnswer`, a `try/catch`, and `rev-parse --verify` before `merge-base`. That is two git spawns per candidate branch instead of one.\n   - It also relies on matching `/failed$/` against the error message to detect \"exit 1 with no stderr\". That is brittle, because it only works when git printed nothing.\n   - A cleaner option is to treat a missing ref as \"skip\" without `rev-parse`. For example, run `git for-each-ref --format=%(objectname) refs/remotes/origin/main …` once and loop only over refs that exist. Then a `merge-base` exit 1 is \"no base\" and anything else warns. That drops `gitAnswer` and the message sniffing.\n   - Both `trustedRef` and `configAt` also repeat the \"warn and use the defaults\" wording. A single `fallback(why)` helper would share it.\n   - Check first that `gitTry` has no remaining callers besides `gitInt`.\n\nThe change is otherwise reasonably lean. The tests are targeted, and the TODO edit is accurate.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
