groups":["b80496ad53a5642d","3ece676ec71590d3","71b2495735e2352d","83390b551c016789","2141b142249e70cc","ba29de40a22aea61","54249e0b3bc722b2"],"findings":"## Review: simplification and reuse\n\nI read the diff against the clone. I did not apply or run any of these suggestions, so each is marked **read**.\n\n1. **Drop the separate `timedOut` notes list (group `timeout-marker`, `src/floor.ts:38-39`, `src/floor.ts:132`, `src/signals.ts:154-158`).** The marker already reaches the attention card through the floor reasons: `floorFrom` puts `pattern: X (timed out: counted as matching)` into `floor.reasons`, and `derived.reasons` carries those too. `Analysis.timedOut`, `timedOutNotes`, `timedOutNote`, `CommitData.computed.timedOut`, `AttentionView.timedOut`, `timedOutLines` and the `timedout` HTML block then repeat the same fact through a second path. The cost is about six places that must stay in sync. The author's stated reason for a separate list is that damped hits are excluded from it. But the floor reasons are built from `live`, which already excludes damped hits, so they have the same scope. Removing the separate path should keep the attention card's \"timed out\" line, but this needs a check that the existing test still passes. **Read.** Benefit: the largest one, roughly 30 lines and one concept fewer. Size: medium.\n\n2. **Reuse the existing reasons list in the HTML card (`src/html/client.js:243-247`, `src/html/style.css:168`).** If the timed-out text is kept, append it to the `reasons` list that is already rendered (the `ul` at line ~240) instead of creating a new `ul` with a new `.timedout` class and CSS rule. The text and sentence are the same kind, so the separate block adds nothing. **Read.** Size: small (about 5 lines and 1 CSS line).\n\n3. **Make the sort in `floorFrom` simpler (`src/signals.ts:166-170`).** `[...top.filter((x) => x.timedOut), ...top.filter((x) => !x.timedOut)]` is a two-pass stable partition. It is equivalent to `[...top].sort((a, b) => Number(!!b.timedOut) - Number(!!a.timedOut))` (Array sort is stable in modern JS), and it is clearer about intent. The `label` helper is only used once, so it can be inlined. **Read.** Small benefit, small change.\n\n4. **Inline `timedOutNote` (`src/signals.ts:154`).** It is exported but used only once, inside `timedOutNotes`. If suggestion 1 is taken, this disappears with it. If not, inline it. **Read.** Trivial.\n\n5. **`trustedRef` (`src/config.ts`, the `for` loop).** The `rev-parse --verify -q` pre-check exists only to tell \"no such branch\" (exit 1) from a failing `merge-base` (exit 128). That is a real need, and the code is correct as written. I considered a single `merge-base` call with a special case for exit 128, but that is more fragile, so I would leave it. I found no better reuse: `gitTry` returns null on any failure, which is exactly what this change is trying to stop doing.\n\nNot suggested: the `warnOnce` set and `gitAnswer`. They are small and each has one clear job. The `GitError.status` field is needed by `gitAnswer`, so it is not extra.\n\nScope: the diff's main cost is the timed-out marker plumbing (suggestions 1 to 4). The git-failure group is already lean.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
